Here is the commit message:
fixing errors: * Not able to unmount filesystem * Wrongly set
 isMounted variable during shutdown

Here is the root cause:
The original code called `NativeMethods.DokanMain(...)` synchronously, but this native call is blocking and only returns once the filesystem has actually been unmounted. As a result, `isMounted.set(true)` was executed only after `DokanMain` returned — i.e., after the filesystem was already unmounted — meaning `isMounted` never correctly reflected the "currently mounted" state while the filesystem was active. Consequently, when `shutdown()` was called, it read `isMounted.get()` as `false` (since the flag was never properly set to `true` during the active mount), causing it to skip the actual `DokanRemoveMountPoint` unmount call, or incorrectly log/behave as if the device was already unmounted. Additionally, in `shutdown()`, `isMounted` was directly overwritten with the boolean result of `DokanRemoveMountPoint`, so a failed unmount attempt would incorrectly set `isMounted` to `false` even though the filesystem was still mounted, further corrupting the mount-state tracking. The fix wraps the blocking `DokanMain` call in an asynchronous task with a timeout so the mount status can be properly determined without blocking, and it decouples the shutdown success/failure branches so `isMounted` is only updated to `false` when the unmount truly succeeds.

